2. h_ml = 35.25: IS THE GAIN PRIOR CREDIT OR LIKELIHOOD? (the 08-28 test)
========================================================================
[ccx_adopt_mode_band] h_ml band -> [30, 200]; h_ml at the mode = 35.2523 m
[ccx_adopt_mode_band] h_ml band -> [85, 120]; h_ml at the mode = 96.4737 m
  refit  from90   h_ml   35.25  fert_k  189.218   logpost  -1547.158 = prior  -52.287 + loglik   -1494.871
  incumbent       h_ml   96.47  fert_k  154.845   logpost  -1586.766 = prior  -58.932 + loglik   -1527.833

  DELTA (refit - incumbent):  logpost  +39.608 = prior  +6.645 + loglik  +32.962
  08-28 REJECTED refit, same split:   +4.060 = prior  +7.397 + loglik   -1.199

  ⚠ VERDICT: THE 08-28 REJECTION CRITERION DOES NOT APPLY HERE. That mode was
    rejected because its gain was PRIOR CREDIT bought with a WORSE likelihood.
    This one's prior credit is comparable (+6.6 vs +7.4) but its LIKELIHOOD
    IMPROVES BY +33.0 rather than degrading. A shallow h_ml is not the verdict;
    the split is, and here it points the other way.
  ⚠ WHAT THIS DOES NOT SAY: most of that +33.0 is RECOVERING the adoption's own
    cost -- the incumbent is a pre-adoption vector read under a post-adoption
    objective. The claim is 'the refit is likelihood-driven', NOT 'h_ml = 35.25
    is vindicated'. Isolating h_ml needs a PROFILE at the new mode.

